This is a copy of github.com/cloudsoda/go-smb2 at
v0.0.0-20261105190815-95be04a983b8 (BSD License, see LICENSE),
used by BackupZit through a replace directive in its go.mod.
The upstream tests are kept (go test ./... in this folder); its .github
folder (CI with a Samba server) is left out.

Changes by BackupZit that upstream does not have (2026-11-25):
- client.go: File.readAt keeps up to four READ requests (pipelineDepth)
  in flight and copies each response to its place, instead of waiting
  for each 1 MiB chunk's response before sending the next request.
  Credits are borrowed per request as before; an error or the end of the
  file stops sending, and the requests still in flight are drained.
- pipeline_test.go: tests and benchmarks of the above against an
  in-process server that answers after a fixed latency.

Drop this copy once upstream has these changes.
